TI  - Chylothorax From Gorham-Stout Disease.
PG  - 340-342
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000506 [doi]
AB  - Chylothorax is one of the presenting features in many disorders including 
      malignancy. Thorough investigation is often required for establishing the 
      etiology of chylothorax. Unfortunately, despite appropriate work-up etiology of 
      pleural effusion cannot be established. We report a case of chylothorax 
      associated with multiple lytic bony lesions, finally diagnosed as a case of 
      Gorham-Stout disease.
