TI  - Tracheal squamous cell carcinoma treated endoscopically.
PG  - 353-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181f1e809 [doi]
AB  - Malignant primary tracheal tumors are extremely rare. The most common malignant 
      primary tracheal tumors are squamous cell carcinoma and adenoid cystic 
      carcinomas. In this brief report, we describe a patient who presented with a 
      primary papillary squamous cell carcinoma in-situ at multiple areas in the 
      trachea with a significant airway obstruction. Our case was successfully managed 
      using a combination of electrocautery and argon photocoagulation for endotracheal 
      ablation of the tumor and adjuvant external beam radiotherapy.
