TI  - Tracheobronchial rhinoscleroma.
PG  - 283-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181be3074 [doi]
AB  - Rhinoscleroma is a chronic infectious disease caused by Klebsiella 
      rhinoscleromatis. It initially involves the nasal cavity and can occasionally 
      extend to the rest of the upper respiratory tract. We report a case of 
      rhinoscleroma involving both the larynx and the tracheobronchial tree, presenting 
      with recurrent respiratory infection.
