TI  - Pneumomediastinum complicating transbronchial needle aspiration.
PG  - 193-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181afd466 [doi]
AB  - Transbronchial needle aspiration (TBNA) is a safe procedure with a reported 
      complication rate of less than 1%. Pneumomediastinum after TBNA has not been 
      reported in the English literature in the past. We present the case of a 
      65-year-old woman with widely metastatic small cell carcinoma, who developed 
      pneumomediastinum after flexible bronchoscopy with TBNA. A persistent visible 
      defect in the bronchial wall at the site of the needle insertion strongly 
      implicated the TBNA as the cause of the pneumomediastinum.
