TI  - Methylene Blue for Bronchopleural Fistula Localization.
PG  - 63-66
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000423 [doi]
AB  - A bronchopleural fistula (BPF) is a communication between the pleural space and 
      the bronchial tree. BPFs are challenging to diagnose and are associated with a 
      high morbidity and mortality. Sequential balloon occlusion is commonly used for 
      localization of a BPF. We describe our experience with 4 cases of successful 
      localization of the BPF by instillation of methylene blue into the pleural space 
      through a pigtail catheter, with simultaneous bronchoscopic visualization of dye 
      in the tracheobronchial tree. Two patients were treated with endobronchial valves 
      and 3 had a surgical thoracic muscle flap placed.
