DP  - 2015 Apr
TI  - New cancer or carcinoid progression to small cell lung cancer?
PG  - 186-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000147 [doi]
AB  - Carcinoids and small cell lung cancer share neuroendocrine cellular origins. 
      Surgery is the definitive treatment in typical carcinoid with few recurrences. 
      For patients considered to be poor surgical candidates, ablative and 
      cryotherapies have been utilized with good results. The long-term consequences of 
      these alternatives approaches are unclear. We report a case of typical carcinoid 
      treated with various alternative approaches over a period of 6 years with either 
      transformation to small cell lung cancer or the development of a new primary in 
      the same location.
