TI  - A leech at the aerodigestive crossroads.
PG  - 173-4
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000156 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of hemoptysis observed in a 32-year-old man with an uneventful 
      past history. Flexible bronchoscopy demonstrated presence of a leech attached to 
      the laryngeal orifice. This condition is common in endemic areas but is 
      underdiagnosed. The association of hemoptysis, voice alterations, and difficult 
      respiration are suggestive signs. Extraction should be achieved rapidly to avoid 
      death from asphyxiation or acute respiratory failure.
