TI  - Endobronchial occlusion for massive hemoptysis with a guidewire-assisted 
      custom-made silicone spigot: a new technique.
PG  - 366-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000106 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial Watanabe spigot is a device used to occlude bronchus for a variety 
      of indications. It has been recently used for endobronchial occlusion for 
      hemoptysis. However, its application is not always easy, particularly if the 
      bleeding is originating from the upper lobes. To facilitate its placement, we 
      developed a new technique using a guidewire and a custom-made spigot. We report a 
      case of massive hemoptysis from a left lung cancer describing this new approach.
