VI  - 20
IP  - 1
DP  - 2013 Jan
TI  - Obstructive fibrinous tracheal pseudomembrane.
PG  - 63-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e318281a332 [doi]
AB  - Obstructive fibrinous tracheal pseudomembrane (OFTP) is a relatively rare cause 
      of failed extubation. OFTP may be more common than described in the literature. 
      OFTP results from ischemic injury to tracheal mucosa and may be the initial stage 
      of the development of tracheal stenosis. Early diagnosis and treatment can 
      prevent re intubation and mortality. We present a rare case of OFTP. The patient 
      was intubated for 3 days for asthma exacerbation and was appropriately 
      discharged. The patient was seen the second time in the emergency room and was 
      treated for asthma exacerbation on the same day. Because of persistent symptoms 
      after 3 days, CT scan of the chest was performed, which indicated necrotizing 
      tracheitis with gas formation within the tracheal wall. Bronchoscopy showed no 
      evidence of necrosis, but there was a thick white plaque toughly adherent to the 
      tracheal wall.
