TI  - Reversible bronchiectasis in an adult: a case report.
PG  - 336-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31826ca79d [doi]
AB  - Bronchiectasis is classically defined as irreversible bronchial dilatation that 
      represents the sequelae of chronic airway inflammation and is permanent, 
      reflecting the presence of bronchiectasis. It is increasingly being recognized 
      with the wider availability of high-resolution computed tomography. In contrast 
      to adults, children with noncystic fibrosis bronchiectasis may have resolution or 
      significant improvement in bronchial dilatation. We report a case of reversible 
      bronchial dilatation in an adult as evidenced by high-resolution computed 
      tomography, which demonstrates that, although quite rare in adults, spontaneous 
      resolution may occur.
