TI  - Bronchoesophageal fistula.
PG  - 47-9
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31823fc99e [doi]
AB  - Bronchoesophageal fistula (BEF) is an undesirable consequence of esophageal 
      cancer. A BEF is encountered in 5% to 15% of patients with esophageal cancer. It 
      is generally a life-threatening complication because of the development of 
      recurrent pulmonary infection and sepsis. We present a case with esophageal 
      cancer and acquired BEF. The fistula allowed herniation of the esophageal wall 
      into the endobronchial lumen, causing significant obstruction of the airway 
      lumen, findings not reported previously.
