TI  - Endotracheal bronchogenic cyst.
PG  - 340-2
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3182310d41 [doi]
AB  - A 68-year-old woman was admitted with symptoms of dry cough and stridor. Computed 
      tomography of the chest revealed a cystic, polypoid lesion protruding inside the 
      trachea, extending to the subcarina. The patient underwent a resection of the 
      cyst, which was found to penetrate the wall of the trachea. Most commonly, 
      bronchogenic cysts appear in the medial one third of the lungs or in the 
      mediastinum. This is a rare case of a mediastinal bronchogenic cyst protruding 
      into the trachea.
