TI  - An endobronchial lipoma: diagnosis remains a challenge.
PG  - 95-6
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181ce08fb [doi]
AB  - Benign tumors of the endobronchial tree are rare, and among them endobronchial 
      lipoma is the least common. It is histologically benign in character but may 
      cause bronchial obstruction. We describe a case of a 68-year-old woman with an 
      endobronchial lipoma arising in the left lower lobe bronchus who had been treated 
      for frequent chest infections for the past 3 years.
