TI  - Bronchial mucoepidermoid carcinoma: an unusual cause of complex cystic lung mass 
      in a young man.
PG  - 73-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181ccb085 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial mucopeidermoid carcinoma is extremely rare, with an incidence of 0.1 to 
      0.2% of all primary lung tumors. It usually presents as an endobronchial mass 
      with either partial or total occlusion of the airway lumen. Common clinical 
      presentations are hemoptysis, airway obstruction, and recurrent atelectasis or 
      pneumonia. We present a 27-year-old man who complained of chronic cough as a 
      result of bronchial mucopeidermoid carcinoma with resultant obstructive lung 
      changes.
