LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31819c100f [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary fistulas are associated with a high risk of morbidity and mortality. We 
      report 2 cases of alveolopleural fistulas, 1 in a patient with chronic 
      hydropneumothorax and the other after wedge biopsy. In both cases, Watanabe 
      spigot (Novatech, Grasse, France) was placed for bronchial occlusion with 
      short-term success.
