TI  - Granular cell tumor of trachea.
PG  - 68-9
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31818fd8c8 [doi]
AB  - Granular cell tumors of the tracheobronchial tree are rare benign lesions of 
      neurogenic origin. These benign tumors mostly involve the skin, oral cavity, or 
      esophagus. There is no consensus regarding treatment of granular cell tumors. 
      Treatment varies from simple observation to different bronchoscopic 
      interventions, such as laser therapy or fulguration to surgical resection.
