DP  - 2018 Oct
TI  - Endobronchial Myxoma: An Uncommon Entity.
PG  - 335-339
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000503 [doi]
AB  - A 31-year-old woman presented with progressive breathlessness since 1 year. 
      Flexible bronchoscopy revealed a vascular tumor completely occluding the right 
      main bronchus. A diagnosis of primary endobronchial myxoma was made. Tumor 
      debulking was performed using rigid bronchoscopy. This enabled right lower 
      lobectomy. A literature search yielded 12 cases of primary pulmonary myxoma, and 
      only 2 previous reports of endobronchial myxoma. Most tumors were incidentally 
      detected and were cured surgically. Endobronchial myxomas are rare and are 
      usually asymptomatic. Treatment involves surgical excision. Rigid bronchoscopy 
      serves as a bridge to surgery and can reduce the extent of surgery.
