TI  - Inflammatory pseudotumor of the pleura.
PG  - 154-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000070 [doi]
AB  - Inflammatory pseudotumors are rare solid, non-neoplastic masses that can mimic 
      pulmonary malignancy. It occurs most commonly in children and young adults and is 
      usually found incidentally. There are many reports of the existence of this tumor 
      in various organs in the human body. The occurrence of this tumor exclusively in 
      the pleura has not been described before. We present a case of inflammatory 
      pseudotumor of the pleura and its successful management.
