TI  - Acute Exacerbation of Interstitial Lung Disease After Cryobiopsy.
PG  - 319-322
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000369 [doi]
AB  - Cryotherapy has been used in treatment of lung cancer for decades. The utility of 
      cryotechnology in diagnosis of lung diseases is emerging and gaining popularity. 
      Cryobiopsy (CB) of the lung, when compared with conventional transbronchial 
      forceps lung biopsy, has proposed to have a higher diagnostic yield in 
      interstitial lung disease by providing larger biopsy specimen and less crush 
      artifact. Acute exacerbation of interstitial lung disease (AEILD) has been well 
      described with surgical lung biopsies and, rarely, with conventional 
      transbronchial forceps biopsy. The incidence of AEILD after CB is not known. Here 
      we are presenting a case of AEILD after CB.
