TI  - Transesophageal Bronchoscopic Ultrasound-Guided Fine-Needle Aspiration for 
      Metastatic Vertebral Body Lesion.
PG  - 156-158
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000235 [doi]
AB  - Malignant neoplasms frequently cause vertebral metastases. Traditionally, either 
      image-guided percutaneous biopsy or open biopsy has been performed for sampling 
      specimens for the definitive diagnosis. We herein report a case with suspected 
      multiple metastases but unknown primary, who underwent endobronchial 
      ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration for mediastinal lymph nodes 
      with negative results by rapid onsite cytologic evaluation, followed by the 
      transesophageal approach with the ultrasound bronchoscope for the vertebral body 
      lesion at the same setting that provided a definitive diagnosis of metastatic 
      hepatocellular carcinoma.
