TI  - Localized Pleural Metastases of Renal Cell Carcinoma After Nephrectomy: A Case 
      Report and Literature Review.
PG  - 59-62
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000181 [doi]
AB  - We herein report the case of a 61-year-old Japanese male with localized pleural 
      metastases of renal cell carcinoma. The patient was admitted to our hospital 
      because of dyspnea on exertion and left-sided pleural effusion. He had undergone 
      right radical nephrectomy 10 years previously. Contrast-enhanced whole-body 
      computed tomography revealed scattered nodular thickening of the left pleura with 
      contrast enhancement and left-sided pleural effusion. Thoracoscopy performed 
      under local anesthesia was applied to obtain a biopsy of the pleural nodules, and 
      the specimen was consequently diagnosed as exhibiting pleural metastasis of renal 
      cell carcinoma, clear cell type.
