TI  - Pulmonary Neuroendocrine Tumors: Part II. Treatment.
PG  - 351-6
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000206 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary neuroendocrine tumors that arise from Kulchitzky cells of the bronchial 
      mucosa consist of a spectrum of histologic features leading to a variable 
      prognosis. Although typical carcinoid represents the most benign course, 
      small-cell cancer has the grimmest outcome. Therefore, differentiating the 
      spectrum of neuroendocrine tumors helps one not only to determine the prognosis, 
      but also to guide the treatment options. In this part, we aim to discuss the 
      treatment options in pulmonary neuroendocrine tumors except for small-cell lung 
      cancer.
