DP  - 2013 Jul
TI  - Use of linear EBUS in work-up of a pulmonary nodule.
PG  - 278-80
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31829dfe58 [doi]
AB  - Diagnostic approach to a pulmonary nodule depends upon the characteristics of the 
      nodule and its location. Despite utilizing advanced minimally invasive diagnostic 
      techniques, the work-up might be challenging. We report the case of a 60-year-old 
      woman with history of breast cancer that was treated with lumpectomy 11 years 
      earlier. She presented with a pulmonary nodule located medially in the fissure 
      between the left upper and lower lobes. Linear EBUS was chosen as a diagnostic 
      approach and the diagnosis of metastatic breast cancer was made without any 
      complications. This case highlights the potential use of linear EBUS in centrally 
      located pulmonary nodules or masses.
