TI  - A young woman with recurrent lower respiratory tract infection.
PG  - 35-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31827cca5f [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchomegaly is a rare congenital abnormality with marked widening of the 
      trachea and major bronchi, in most cases associated with chronic recurrent 
      respiratory tract infection. We present this rare syndrome in a young woman who 
      presented with recurrent respiratory tract infection. She was found to have 
      tracheobronchomegaly on flexible bronchoscopy, which was confirmed with 
      high-resolution computed tomography findings.
