TI  - Primary mucoepidermoid carcinoma of the lung.
PG  - 203-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31825c6c30 [doi]
AB  - Mucoepidermoid carcinoma (MEC) of the lung is a rare endobronchial tumor 
      accounting for up to 0.2% of primary lung cancer. We report a patient with MEC 
      who presented with cough, hemoptysis, and localized findings on chest 
      examination. This case emphasizes the importance of obtaining adequate biopsy to 
      establish the correct diagnosis. In addition, it highlights that MEC of the lung 
      usually presents in the low-grade form, carrying a favorable prognosis.
