TI  - Endotracheal spindle cell lipoma presenting as a chronic cough.
PG  - 105-7
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31819b2724 [doi]
AB  - An elderly gentleman with a chronic cough was found to have a large midtracheal 
      lesion on computed tomography scan. Endotracheal extirpation with an 
      electrocautery snare successfully removed the lesion. Histologic and 
      immunohistochemical analyses revealed the lesion to be a spindle cell lipoma. We 
      provide herein the case presentation and management, the differential diagnosis, 
      and an overview of spindle cell lipoma.
