TI  - Tracheal web: presentation of a case with uncommon features.
PG  - 46-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181908c5d [doi]
AB  - Postintubation tracheal web is a rarely encountered complication of endotracheal 
      intubation. Although few of them remain asymptomatic until diagnosed 
      accidentally, most of them present with symptoms of acute airway obstruction and 
      even death. We present here a case of postintubation tracheal web with uncommon 
      features, including a very long delay in diagnosis despite a 99% obstruction of 
      the tracheal lumen.
